adduser
Definition

adduser is a high-level, interactive command that creates a new user account and automatically performs tasks such as creating the home directory and prompting for a password.

useradd is a low-level command used to create a user. It does not prompt for additional information and requires you to specify options.  sudo useradd [options] username

Create a user with a home directory: sudo useradd -m siva    Without -m, a home directory may not be created.
Set a password: sudo passwd siva
Common useradd Options
Option	Description
-m	Create home directory
-d	Specify home directory
-s	Specify login shell
-u	Specify user ID (UID)
-g	Specify primary group

Example: sudo useradd -m -s /bin/bash siva
Verify the User
id siva

or

cat /etc/passwd | grep siva
