passwd [options] username
passwd (Password) is a Linux command used to set, change, or manage a user's password.
Option                    	Description
passwd username	         Set/change another user's password (root)
passwd                	Change your own password
-l	Lock a user account
-u	Unlock a user account
-e	Expire the password (change required at next login)
-S	Display password status
  
passwd                Change your own password
sudo passwd siva      Change another user's password
sudo passwd -l siva   Lock a user account 
sudo passwd -u siva   Unlock a user account
sudo passwd -e siva   Force password change at next login
sudo passwd -S siva    Check password status



















